Summary:
During today’s session, the focus was on improving the overall performance of the Developer Portfolio Evaluator application. We reviewed both frontend and backend processes to identify areas where efficiency could be enhanced. Optimizations were made in API handling to reduce unnecessary operations and improve response time. Minor refinements were also applied to the frontend to ensure smoother rendering and better user interaction. The application was tested multiple times to observe performance improvements and ensure stability after the changes.

Outcomes:
By the end of the session, the application demonstrated improved responsiveness and faster data processing. Optimized API calls and cleaner logic contributed to reduced delays in fetching and displaying results. The frontend updates resulted in a smoother user experience with quicker updates on user actions. These improvements enhanced the overall efficiency of the system without affecting existing functionality. The session provided better insight into performance optimization techniques in full-stack applications.
